Track 2: ¿Quién cerró el pararrayos?
- Story & Context: Rosa stood in the center of the flooded studio holding a melted fuse, realizing that by closing the master grounding shunt, she had trapped the ghosts of every musician who ever played here during a typhoon. She stared at the rain-lashed glass, asking the empty, cold room the question that defines her madness: "Can you hear the brass sections singing through the wire?"
- Story & Context: The room felt smaller as she realized the shadows on the wall were breathing in time with the percussion, an eternal looping of a performance that never ended.

Track 3: Chitinous Reliquary
- Story & Context: Decades later, the ruins of the studio are known as the reliquary where children find fossilized insect husks that still vibrate at 120 beats per minute. A local mystic claims that if you hold an ear to the floor, you can hear the final, eternal chord of the station’s last broadcast. "We are the shells left behind by the thunder" is the hymn the wind hums through the broken rafters, ensuring the legend never fully decays into the soil.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An abandoned, overgrown broadcast control room filled with floating, iridescent insect husks, beams of ethereal moonlight piercing through a caved-in roof, hauntingly beautiful and surreal.

